# The working tree is deliberately byte-stable across machines.
#
# This repository contains a mix of CRLF and LF files, some of them mixed within
# a single file, and the deployed mod is compared byte-for-byte against the repo
# by tools/verify_install.sh. If git normalised endings on checkout, moving to
# another OS would rewrite thousands of lines, bury real changes in noise, and
# make that comparison meaningless.
#
# So: never convert anything. What is committed is what lands on disk.
* -text

# Binary assets, stated explicitly so no tool guesses.
*.png binary
*.jar binary
*.bin binary
*.pzby binary
*.class binary
graphify-out/graph.json merge=graphify

# Evidence files are MACHINE OUTPUT, not source. A check writes them from a
# real run - tab-separated rows where an empty field leaves trailing spaces -
# and they are the record of what was true at a commit. `git diff --check`
# flags that whitespace, and the only ways to silence it are to edit the
# record or to let the check fail. Neither is acceptable: evidence is not
# rewritten to please a linter, and a whitespace warning must not be the
# reason a verification step reports failure.
docs/management/evidence/** -whitespace
dev/eval/** -whitespace
